<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?><parameters><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_HOSTNAME</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>true</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Base address of your SAP S/4HANA system, including the protocol — for example https://my123456-api.s4hana.cloud.sap. Must start with https://; the flow refuses every request against a plain http:// address so that credentials and business data are never sent unencrypted. The one exception is a system behind an SAP Cloud Connector (proxy type sapcc): there, enter the virtual host defined in the Cloud Connector, written with http:// — for example http://s4hana.virtual:44300. Nothing travels unencrypted, the Cloud Connector's tunnel does the encrypting.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_AUTH_METHOD</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>true</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>How this flow signs in to SAP S/4HANA; choose one of the entries the screen offers. OAuth2 Client Credentials, the shipped default, is the method of a communication arrangement on SAP S/4HANA Cloud that issues a client ID and secret. Basic is a user name and a password, the method for an on-premise or private-edition system and for a system behind an SAP Cloud Connector. Client Certificate signs in with a key pair from this tenant's keystore. The security material named in S4_CREDENTIAL_ALIAS, or the key pair named in S4_PRIVATE_KEY_ALIAS, must be of the matching type.</description>
    <additionalMetadata>
      <isCombobox>true</isCombobox>
    </additionalMetadata>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_CREDENTIAL_ALIAS</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>true</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Name of the security material in this tenant that holds the sign-in details for SAP S/4HANA. Create it under Monitor, Manage Security, Security Material. The material's type must match S4_AUTH_METHOD: OAuth2 Client Credentials for the shipped default, User Credentials for Basic. Not used with Client Certificate.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_PRIVATE_KEY_ALIAS</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Alias of the key pair in this tenant's keystore (Monitor, Manage Security, Keystore) that identifies this tenant to SAP S/4HANA when S4_AUTH_METHOD is Client Certificate. Leave empty for the other methods.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>How long a single call to SAP S/4HANA may take before it is abandoned, in milliseconds. The flow makes one attempt and answers 504 when this passes, which the calling application then retries; keep the value below that application's own timeout so it receives the 504 rather than a dropped connection. Keboola's SAP OData component waits 60 seconds unless its own timeout setting says otherwise.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_PROXY_TYPE</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>How this tenant reaches your SAP S/4HANA system. Use default when the system is reachable over the internet, or sapcc when it sits behind an SAP Cloud Connector. Where the screen offers a list, these are its entries Internet and On-Premise.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_CC_LOCATION_ID</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Location identifier of the SAP Cloud Connector to use. Leave empty unless you run more than one Cloud Connector against this tenant and set the proxy type to sapcc.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>AIR_KEY</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Integration key issued by SAP for this package, sent with every call so SAP can recognise the integration. Leave empty unless the documentation of this package gives you a key.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>AIR_HEADER_NAME</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Name of the request header the integration key is sent in, as stated in the instructions SAP supplies with the key. Nothing is sent unless both this and the key are filled in.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>S4_SAP_CLIENT</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Client number of the SAP system to sign in to, for example 100. Needed only on an on-premise or private-edition system with more than one client; leave empty for SAP S/4HANA Cloud and for single-client systems. When set it is sent as sap-client with every call.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>SENDER_ROLE</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>true</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>User role a caller must hold to reach this endpoint; the platform checks it before the flow runs and answers 403 without a log entry when it is missing. ESBMessaging.send, the shipped value, is held by every integration client of this tenant. To open the endpoint to Keboola alone, create a role of your own under Monitor, Manage Security, User Roles, grant it to the service instance whose key Keboola uses, and name it here.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><parameter>
    <key/>
    <name>CONNECTOR_PATH_PREFIXES</name>
    <type>xsd:string</type>
    <isRequired>false</isRequired>
    <constraint/>
    <description>Comma separated list of path prefixes this connector forwards to SAP S/4HANA; a request for a path outside them is answered 403 PATH_NOT_ALLOWED and never reaches SAP. Ships with the roots of SAP's OData V2 and V4 services. Add a prefix for a service that lives elsewhere; leave empty to forward every path, so that only the communication user's authorizations limit what can be read.</description>
    <additionalMetadata/>
  </parameter><param_references><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::httpAddressWithoutQuery" attribute_uilabel="Address" param_key="S4_HOSTNAME"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_HOSTNAME"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::authenticationMethod" attribute_uilabel="Authentication" param_key="S4_AUTH_METHOD"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::credentialName" attribute_uilabel="Credential Name" param_key="S4_CREDENTIAL_ALIAS"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_CREDENTIAL_ALIAS"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::privateKeyAlias" attribute_uilabel="Private Key Alias" param_key="S4_PRIVATE_KEY_ALIAS"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::httpRequestTimeout" attribute_uilabel="Timeout (in ms)" param_key="HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::proxyType" attribute_uilabel="Proxy Type" param_key="S4_PROXY_TYPE"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_PROXY_TYPE"/><reference attribute_category="Receiver" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTP/tp::HTTP/mp::None/direction::Receiver/version::1.17.0/attrId::locationID" attribute_uilabel="Location ID" param_key="S4_CC_LOCATION_ID"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_CC_LOCATION_ID"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="AIR_KEY"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="AIR_HEADER_NAME"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="S4_SAP_CLIENT"/><reference attribute_category="Sender" attribute_id="ctype::AdapterVariant/cname::HTTPS/tp::HTTPS/mp::None/direction::Sender/version::1.5.2/attrId::userRole" attribute_uilabel="User Role" param_key="SENDER_ROLE"/><reference attribute_category="FlowElement" attribute_id="ctype::FlowstepVariant/cname::Enricher/version::1.6.3/attrId::propertyTable" attribute_uilabel="Exchange Property" param_key="CONNECTOR_PATH_PREFIXES"/></param_references></parameters>